<title>POLAND: POLISH SHARES CLOSE LOWER IN CONTINUOUS TRADE.</title>
<headline>POLISH SHARES CLOSE LOWER IN CONTINUOUS TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seven stocks fell, two rose and eight were flat in 7.9-million-zloty Warsaw bourse continuous trade on Tuesday with the WIG 20 index closing at 1,617.6 points, 1.2 percent lower than at the regular session.</p>
<p>The remaining six stocks did not trade.</p>
<p>NFI units fell 1.3 percent in a 10.8-million-zloty turnover.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
